    "body": "claimed: roer70 · 2026-11-17 20:14 UTC · branch roer70:issue/2374-machine-names-its-post · plan:\n\n1. post: `Machine.post: Option<String>` read from `controller.post` in `parse_mch` (`#[serde(default)]`, no `PROJECT_VERSION` bump).\n2. app: `validate_text` refuses an unknown name and a post of the wrong kind by `controller.post`; `post_offer` offers the mounted machine's named post when it differs from the setup's registry post, and never offers over a `.cps` file post. The banner says why it offers. Taking the offer goes through the existing `SelectPostNamed`, so a mount never changes the post by itself.\n3. assets: the shipped machines with a written pairing state their post; `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` documents the key.\n4. The tests listed in the issue. Gate quick, then gate batch, then gate release before ready.\n\nThe pairing goes in the `.mch` file as proposed. If you'd rather have a table in code, say so before the PR.",
