    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T04:00:33Z",
    "body": "Seen again by a QA run (SolidCraft v0.44.1 + CamCraft v0.23.0, part p01-flange; re-checked on upstream main abe24ff09): after `load_machine {builtin: \"Tormach 770MX\"}`, `get_job` reports `\"posts_with\": \"Fanuc (built-in)\"` for the setup, and a plain `post` writes Fanuc output (`%`, `O0001`, `G91 G28 Z0`) for the 770MX. `post {post: \"Tormach PathPilot\"}` works, but the choice is not stored unless `set_setup_post` is used.\n\nOne more MCP detail for the fix: the `post` tool's `post` parameter description lists \"Fanuc, Haas, Siemens 840D, Heidenhain, Mazak, Tormach PathPilot Plasma\" - it leaves out \"Tormach PathPilot\" (and the newer grblHAL / TinyG / Carvera posts), so an agent driving a Tormach mill does not learn the right name from the tool list.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
