    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T10:45:12Z",
    "body": "Good QA finding. I add the MCP part to this issue, on the same branch:\n\n- `load_machine` replies with `post_offer` for the setup that it mounted to: the post that the machine names, why, and the `set_setup_post` call that takes it. The mount does not change the post.\n- `get_job` gives `post_offer` for each setup, next to `posts_with`. `null` means no offer.\n- The description of the `post` tool lists every name in `BUILTINS`. Thus \"Tormach PathPilot\", grblHAL, TinyG and the Carvera posts are in the list.\n\nPinned by `crates/app/tests/mcp_machine_post.rs`, which includes your 770MX case: Fanuc stays until `set_setup_post`, and undo brings Fanuc back.\n\nThe `post` tool's `post` parameter stays a one-time choice. It does not store the post, so `set_setup_post` is the call that keeps it.",
